{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to put each new or changed requirement into a group, where a group holds requirements that cite each other or describe one feature. It MUST direct them to review every group with its own read-only subagent, with all the reviews running in parallel, before presenting any group to the user.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement obligates the `habeas-requirements` skill to direct agents to do four things:\n1. Put each new or changed requirement into a group.\n2. Define a group as requirements that cite each other or describe one feature.\n3. Review every group with its own read-only subagent, with all the reviews running in parallel.\n4. Do those reviews before presenting any group to the user.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_reviews_each_group_with_a_parallel_read_only_subagent]` covers all four:\n- It finds the workflow step by `step_of(SKILL, \"start a read-only subagent\")`. That call panics if no step mentions a read-only subagent.\n- It asserts the whitespace-collapsed step text contains \"Sort the new and changed requirements into groups\". This covers the obligation to group each requirement.\n- It asserts the step text contains \"requirements that cite each other or describe one feature\". This covers the group definition.\n- It asserts the step text contains \"For each group, start a read-only subagent, all in parallel\". This covers one read-only subagent per group, running in parallel.\n- It asserts `review < step_of(SKILL, \"Present each group to the user\")`. This covers the review coming before any group is presented.\n\nThe helpers `step_of`, `step`, `workflow_steps`, `collapse` and `assert_text` make these assertions effective. `workflow_steps` collapses wrapped lines, so phrases match across line breaks. `assert_text` fails if any phrase is missing. The skill step in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` (step 3) contains these phrases.\n\nThe tests don't need to exercise any other case, because the requirement text names no other boundary or mode.",
  "references": "870297c9f5d32fd4392ee702cceaad8f5902189885c67ac640b021452e5d913b",
